        ],
        "statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. The bounded region of a smooth embedded\ncircle in the oriented plane, together with its boundary, is a smooth manifold\nwith boundary diffeomorphic to the closed standard disk. Let $D_0,D_1$ be two\nsuch closed regions. Every orientation-preserving smooth boundary\ndiffeomorphism $b:\\partial D_0\\to\\partial D_1$ extends to an\norientation-preserving diffeomorphism $B:D_0\\to D_1$. More precisely, for\nspecified smooth inward collars $c_i:\\partial D_i\\times[0,\\epsilon)\\to D_i$\nwith $c_i(p,0)=p$, the extension may be required to satisfy\n$B(c_0(p,r))=c_1(b(p),r)$ for every sufficiently small $r\\ge0$. In addition, given interior points $p_i\\in D_i$ and an orientation-preserving smooth diffeomorphism $q$ from a neighborhood of $p_0$ onto a neighborhood of $p_1$, the extension can agree with $q$ near $p_0$ while retaining the prescribed boundary collars.",
        "proof_strategy": "direct",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-generated"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "C. T. C. Wall, Differential Topology, Theorem 2.4.2 and Sections 2.6–2.7",
              "url": "https://www.math.auckland.ac.nz/~hekmati/Books/Wall.pdf",
              "locator": "Theorem 2.4.2, printed pp.50–51 (PDF pp.58–59); corner straightening and gluing, printed pp.59–67 (PDF pp.67–75), especially Proposition 2.7.6, printed pp.66–67: boundary sum with a disk preserves the diffeomorphism type. The smooth Jordan reduction and prescribed collar/interior germ constructions are proved locally here."
